  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "xeeOxSOc+rQq/gMYXK20TVWXd6w=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:29:45.961Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Berenschot is vendor-neutral and has no build capability, so the value in the relationship is framework and referral only. It can shape how a Dutch buyer frames a problem and it can make introductions; it cannot implement anything.\n\nThat is worth stating plainly because advisory firms are easy to over-rate in a lead list: they turn up near every interesting decision without ever being the party that acts. The realistic ask of Berenschot is that its frameworks and its introductions point somewhere useful. Priority 4 reflects that \u2014 it stays in the set as a referral route rather than as a delivery candidate.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**4 \u00b7 needs OSS screen**\n- Berenschot (NL)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> Framework and referral value only.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:29:45.961543Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:29:45.961548Z"
    }
  },
